{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/975648-questions-regarding-the-abyssal-worshippers","id":975648,"title":"Questions regarding the Abyssal worshippers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-24T12:35:11-07:00","id":975648,"title":"Questions regarding the Abyssal worshippers","content":"As always, I am sorry if this has been answered in the past. Also, I don't have the sourcebook on Left-Hand Legacies, so... you know. Anyway, I plan to include the Scelesti in my game and want to make them more than just moving targets, so:<br /> <br /> 1. I have entertained the idea that when a mage becomes a Scelestus, his Path becomes corrupted, much like the toxic shamans of &quot;Shadowrun&quot;. A different, more malevolent aspect of that Path becomes apparent, changing the mage's personality and Nimbus. For example, a Thyrsus changes from &quot;run wild and free&quot; to &quot;an atavistic monster that will eat you&quot;. Do you have any ideas on how the Paths might corrupt and how to present that during play? Can becoming a Scelestus influence mage's spellcasting and if yes: in what way?<br /> <br /> 2. The Scelesti need constant influx of new members, mainly because everyone hates their guts and there is a milion ways their magic can go wrong. Why would anyone want to become one? Assuming the potential recruit is relatively sane, what endgame other than &quot;A Thing From Outer Space Eats Your Brain&quot; can they expect? How would you sell a Scelesti agenda to a guy/girl who has been taught ever since his/her Awakening that you are a bunch of mad demon-worshippers? How can Virtues and Vices (from the World of Darkness, not Chronicles of Darkness) affect that approach?<br /> <br /> 3. On a more specific note, I need an antagonist. An Abyssal being (although a spirit or a demon will do, too) of Rank 5 or higher that can possess a living host. An embodiment of all things carnal: lust, slaughter, birth, the works. Preferably of female form. I haven't come across a being this powerful in any of the sourcebooks I know of, so if you have any suggestions (from CofD, other RPGs, books, movies or your own) I will welcome them. Also, I would be extremely grateful for any kind of &quot;inspirational art&quot; for Mage.<br /> <br /> Thank you all in advance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T14:56:00-07:00","id":975701,"title":"","content":"In order:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1: Left-Hand Path was way ahead of you. The end stage of Abyssal magic addiction is being sent on an Abyssal Awakening. It can be delayed indefinitely-and often is, as the path to the nadir depends on insane leaps of logic-but a future Joined mage finds their way to the center of their Path's Ziggurat, the Abyssal version of their Watchtower, and told to betray their own nature to break open the way to true symbiosis with the Void. Those who do, you guessed it, develop dark twists on normal Path symbolism-Acanthus invoke tragedy and mythical betrayal, Thrysus become cynical plastic shamans, Mastigos spurn the world and obliterate the self. The general theme is &quot;open defiance of sane, respectful magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. Both LHP and Imperial Mysteries have more, but the lure of the Abyss is that as an impossibility, it offers things that are likewise impossible. Things like an easy way to return the dead to life, or truly sacrosanct freedom, or a Shadow that isn't an animistic Darwinian hellscape. You want something you feel that the world needs to be broken in order to get, the Void is selling. Also, Scelesti don't have that high of a turnover rate-true Nihilists are actually a minority, most have more comprehensible motives. Motives that depend on them not being stupid.<br /> <br /> 3. There's not much I can add, but keep in mind the Abyss is Paradox disincarnate: there's going to be a trace of your entity that directly contradicts its own carnality. Summoners has good baselines-the Prince in Tatters is a gulmoth of betrayal that cannot act disloyal or unfairly towards its summoner, the Gears of Chaos are a gulmoth of ordered systems that only acts to dissolve organization and simplify complexity, and (most pertinently) the Courtesan is a succubus that is a joyful and willing victim of sex crimes, even suggesting some exciting ones ze thinks will turn zer summoner on. Intruders also has a potential home for your entity, the astral Temple of Zanak Khan (a pulp writer's rather Orientalist vision of carnal decadence possessed by an Annunaku who works to destroy the dreamer's inhibitions and respect for decency or really respect for anything other than lust).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-24-2016, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T20:45:51-07:00","id":975805,"title":"","content":"About 1, keep in mind that non-Scelesti can easily fall under the &quot;dark side&quot; of their paths. It's not so much a Star Wars deal were there's the light side of magic and the dark side. Every Thyrsus kind of already has &quot;run wild and free&quot; and &quot;atavistic monster&quot; inside of them. And the first one can be just as Abyssally-inspiring as the second. The book actually says Tyler Durden would be Thyrsus, and his whole &quot;topple society and modernity&quot; could certainly be an Abyssal motivation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}